Review the SetLogLevel shell argument report

A scanner flagged the Process.Start in SetLogLevel as a shell command built from
a concatenated argument. The argument is an integer checked to lie between 0
and 3 on the only path that reaches the command, so it is a single digit and
cannot carry shell syntax: not exploitable, and the call is unchanged.
Documented the check in a comment so the next reader does not reopen it.
